            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ray"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good soup on a cold night! I used turkey instead of ground beef to cut calories a bit. Also added navy beans as well as red kidney beans and used a can of diced tomato with a large can of tomato juice.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-22T23:07:14.050Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Loreal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Souper good! I even added a can of Franko American spaghetti with tomato sauce. I know…weird, right? But it was good. One cup of beef bouillon too. We like soupy chili, yum!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-23T22:39:07.738Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wasn’t quite sure what to expect with this recipe, but it turned out well. It definitely needs much more chili powder, and depending on your taste, some hot sauce, sriracha, or a bit of cayenne to offset the sweetness of the tomato flavor. Never would have thought to put tomato soup in chili, but it was helpful to the soup's consistency. I pretty much followed the recipe, but did sub beef broth for the water, and cut that amount in half. It doesn’t say to drain the kidney beans, so I didn’t, and I did add just a bit more potato which I think helps put this in the “soup” category instead of all chili ingredients. Very quick and easy to make, just need to allocate some time to cook down and allow the flavors to meld.",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-09T16:27:46.723Z"
          },
          {
